{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Stacked Bar Chart.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Stacked Bar Chart.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"stacked bar chart stacked bar chart","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Stacked Bar Chart.md","fileName":"Stacked Bar Chart.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Stacked Bar Chart","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 18:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Health Data Visualization]] · [[Exploratory Data Visualization in R]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Health Data Visualization","Exploratory Data Visualization in R","analyzinghealthdatainrforsasusers.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Stacked Bar Chart.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Stacked Bar Chart.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"stacked bar chart stacked bar chart","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Stacked Bar Chart.md","fileName":"Stacked Bar Chart.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Stacked Bar Chart","heading":"Stacked Bar Chart","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A stacked bar chart partitions each bar according to the levels of a second categorical variable. It shows both the size of the primary groups and how the secondary outcome is distributed within them.\n\nThe first segment has a common baseline, while later segments do not, so subtle comparisons can be difficult. Frequencies, proportions, and the intended denominator should therefore be made explicit in the labels or accompanying table.\n\nThe book uses the stacked form to display a second category within each group and contrasts it with filled and dodged variants. That comparison makes the choice of denominator and baseline an explicit design decision.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Health Data Visualization","Exploratory Data Visualization in R","analyzinghealt